# Semicolons Required

- Use semicolons at the end of statements in JavaScript and TypeScript files.
- When updating existing code, keep semicolons consistent with this rule.

```typescript
// ✅ Good
const value = 123;
doWork();

// ❌ Bad
const value = 123
doWork()
```
